  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The charge accumulated on the capacitor connected in the following circuit is ______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></mo><mi>μC</mi></math>.</p><p>(Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c8eb7317-479a-4c7c-be6a-eb879e2cee31.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 153px;\"/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "400",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4d2e6733-c900-4530-9853-479b4ebe6b7e.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 170px;\"/></p><p>Under the balanced condition, the capacitor will act as an open circuit.</p><p>The current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced></math> through the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> resistor is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced></math> through the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> resistor is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>From the above diagram, it can be written that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>×</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>Hence, the charge on the capacitor is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>Q</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>150</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μF</mi><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>400</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μC</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
